# SABOTAGE: WS-ERP E3 (ADR-049 R3) — the rollup hand-edit bypass. BOTH arms of
# the slv_stock_level belt (the marker gate AND the ledger-divergence check)
# are removed from the trigger, so the rollup row — the DERIVED cache —
# becomes freely writable: a hand-edit (or a bug) can land quantities/values
# the ledger never moved, with nothing at the storage layer to refuse it.
# StockLevelSync's own writes still run (they compute FROM the ledger), so the
# R3 green paths keep passing; ONLY the belt red paths flip: a raw write
# without the marker now lands, an armed DIVERGING write now lands, and the
# :hand_edit door is OPEN. The ledger stays append-only and NegativeStock
# stays armed (layered defense); R3's independent divergence read
# (ReconcileStock.divergences/3) is the second net that still exposes a
# hand-edited row — exactly the design's "sabotage = a hand-edit path that
# bypasses the ledger" story.
